/tmp/pds-paper-src/sections/solving.tex:3:\label{sec:solving}
/tmp/pds-paper-src/sections/solving.tex:5:In this section, we give an algorithm for solving \extension{\Pds}.
/tmp/pds-paper-src/sections/solving.tex:6:Our algorithm consists of different phases.
/tmp/pds-paper-src/sections/solving.tex:7:In the first phase, we apply the reduction rules described in \cref{sec:reduction rules}.
/tmp/pds-paper-src/sections/solving.tex:13:We note that these phases are somewhat modular in the sense that one could easily add further reduction rules or that one can replace the algorithm for solving the kernel in the final step.
/tmp/pds-paper-src/sections/solving.tex:17:In the latter case, the preceding application of our reduction rules and splitting into subinstances then helps to find better solutions rather than improving the running time of exact solvers.
