We compare the performance of our solver to the \texttt{MILP} and \texttt{MFN} approach, each with and without preprocessing by the reduction rules.
To assess the performance of our approach with reduction rules, we compute the speedup compared to the lowest run time of the previous approaches without reduction rules.

