+What produces the certificate.  The generator first samples n Boolean values.
+Every generated three-literal clause is then chosen from one of four relative
+sign patterns: all three literals true on the plant, or exactly one of the three
+true, each with probability 1/4.  Thus every clause is satisfied.  These four
+patterns have unbiased one-literal and two-literal moments, suppressing the
+usual majority and pairwise spectral signatures of naive planting.  The CNF is
+made monotone with two input vertices per Boolean variable; selecting exactly n
+inputs while requiring every pair-check forces exactly one input per variable.
