    14	
    15	## What this is and whether to trust it
    16	
    17	The family asks for a fixed-cardinality implicating power dominating set. The
    18	solver receives exactly the IPDS-Extension objects introduced in Thomas Bläsius
    19	and Max Göttlicher, [*An Efficient Algorithm for Power Dominating Set*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.09870):
    20	an undirected graph, directed implication arcs, propagating vertices, and an
    21	excluded/selectable partition. A candidate is checked by exact set operations:
    22	closed-neighborhood domination, implication closure, and the rule that an
    23	observed propagating vertex with exactly one unobserved neighbor observes it.
    24	
    25	Generation is inverse, not solve-then-hide. It samples a Boolean assignment,
    26	draws clauses that it satisfies, turns each Boolean variable into two monotone
    27	input vertices, and applies the paper's Lemma 10 AND/OR gadget. The chosen input
    28	vertices are therefore a certificate by construction. `verify()` never reads
    29	`inst["answer"]`, and accepts any correctly formatted selected set whose exact
    30	observation closure is the whole graph.
    31	
    32	The planting distribution uses the four relative truth patterns `111`, `100`,
    33	`010`, and `001` equally. Consequently every literal and every signed literal
    34	pair has zero planted correlation in expectation. This is the reason the usual
    35	majority and pair-spectral signatures of naive planted SAT are absent; it is
    36	also only a defense against low-order attacks, not a hardness proof.
    37	
    38	## Why Track A is the honest claim
    39	
    40	Section 3.4, Lemma 10 gives a parameterized reduction from Weighted Monotone
    41	Circuit Satisfiability to IPDS-Extension. Lemmas 9, 7, and 3 carry the reduction
    42	to ordinary/simple PDS, and Corollary 11 proves PDS W[P]-complete with respect to
    43	solution size. Shipping uses `k=n=240`, so the parameter grows with the instance
    44	rather than sitting in an easy fixed-`k` regime.
    45	
    46	Worst-case W[P]-completeness does **not** establish hardness of this planted
    47	distribution. The distributional evidence is the measured panel: frequency,
    48	greedy, WalkSAT, signed pair-spectral recovery, and watched-literal DPLL all
    49	failed on 8/8 shipping seeds. DPLL used its full 50,000-node budget on every
